                <pb facs="0123" n="113" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg113"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/888: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Uruguay</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-09">December 9, 1941</date>.<lb/>[Received December
                        9—10:42 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>529. This afternoon the Uruguayan Chamber of Deputies voted unanimously that a
                    message of solidarity be sent the United States House of Representatives. The
                    Chamber also voted unanimously a resolution supporting and approving the
                    Uruguayan Government’s decree of yesterday transmitted in my telegram 523.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
